From: OpenWrt developers
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: bound EEPROM firmware reads by the loaded image size

Factory partitions may be shorter than the vendor sample image. Avoid reading
past the firmware allocation when optional precalibration data is absent.

--- a/mt_wifi/embedded/common/ee_flash.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/embedded/common/ee_flash.c
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ static void flash_bin_read(void *ctrl, UCHAR *p, ULONG a, ULONG b)
 	/*load from request firmware*/
 	os_load_code_from_bin(ad, &buffer, name, &len);
 
-	if (len > 0 && buffer != NULL) {
+	if (buffer != NULL && a <= len && b <= len - a) {
 		os_move_mem(p, buffer + a, b);
 	}
 
